# Text files are normalized to LF in the repository and checked out with
# whatever the platform uses, so a contributor on Windows does not turn
# every line of a file into a change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on a checkout that would otherwise
# convert them, since a CRLF line ending makes an interpreter line
# unusable.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets are left alone. Marking them stops Git from attempting a
# line ending conversion and from offering a meaningless diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary

# The screenshot and the icons are the parts of the repository a reader
# sees first, so they are marked as documentation rather than counted
# toward the language statistics.
docs/* linguist-documentation
icons/* linguist-documentation
